2:T659,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the cheapest way to fit a new kitchen?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Keeping the existing layout, choosing standard-sized cabinets and using cost-effective worktops can reduce labour and material costs. Reusing suitable appliances may also help."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I have a fitted kitchen on a budget without using flat-pack units?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Pre-assembled standard units can still be affordable, although the purchase price and installation time may differ. Compare the complete supply-and-fitting cost rather than the cabinet price alone."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which kitchen worktop is best for a limited budget?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Laminate is often a practical budget option, with many colours and patterns available. Timber can also work, but it needs suitable care around sinks and wet areas."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can I reduce kitchen installation costs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Keep plumbing and electrical points close to their current positions, finalise the design before ordering and request a detailed quote covering preparation, fitting, services and waste removal."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should I replace all my kitchen appliances at once?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not necessarily. Appliances that are reliable, suitable for the new layout and in good condition may be reused, allowing more of the budget to go towards storage or installation."}}]}7:["slug","fitted-kitchen-on-a-budget","d"]
